# Line endings.
#
# Every text file in this repo is stored and checked out as LF, on every
# platform. Without this, cloning onto a machine with core.autocrlf=true
# (Git for Windows sets it by default) rewrites the whole tree to CRLF on
# checkout, and the next commit then reads as a 100%-changed diff on every
# file — which buries whatever actually changed.
#
# Settings this in .gitattributes rather than via `git config` deliberately:
# config is per-clone and has to be remembered on each new machine, whereas
# this travels with the repo and applies everywhere automatically.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — exempt, so conversion can never corrupt them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
